Title: The Lamp
Credit: Written by
Author: R. Mella
Contact: r@example.com

FADE IN:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

The lamp turns. ANNA (30s, salt-worn) climbs the iron stairs, counting.

ANNA
Two hundred and twelve.
(beat)
Always two hundred and twelve.

TOM (O.S.)
You'll wear them out.

She smiles. The beam sweeps the black water, again and again, over the rocks where the old boat broke apart.

CUT TO:

EXT. HARBOUR - DAY

Gulls. Nets. Tom mends one, badly.

ANNA
Leave it.

TOM
Can't.

INT. ROOM 1 - DAY

Something happens in room 1, at some length, so that the page fills up the way a real script's pages do.

ANNA
Line 1.

